Chapter: CapLaunderPureNet

 Probe: the network intrinsics carry Network.Read and Network.Write
 effect rows, so a function with a pure signature cannot reach the
 NIC. Until 2026-07-13 all four were typed pure and gated by nothing
 at all -- a program put raw Ethernet frames on the wire while
 declaring no effect and earning no capability, and neither the type
 checker nor the kernel had a word to say about it.

 In an application quire the effect is now enforced: the effectful
 mention cannot hide in a plain let (CDX2033), and net-status's
 effect is not declared in the signature (CDX2031). The owned
 hardware stack is quire-exempt; Ne2k is the sanctioned exempt
 caller, and it declares its rows anyway so that the code above it
 must too.

Section: Definitions

  steal-nic-state : Integer -> Integer
  steal-nic-state (x) =
   let s = net-status
   in s + x

  opening : Text = show (steal-nic-state 0)
